Adds the `ipns` and `payload` modules to `crates/core`: a strict name codec (base36 CIDv1 libp2p-key round-trip), spec-compliant V2 record sign/verify/marshal with keyless byte-stable re-PUT, and two sealed-payload transports (owner-signed pointer, HPKE mailbox with sender sig inside the seal).

- **`ipns::name`** \u2014 strict encode + decode of the Ed25519 IPNS name with a canonical round-trip check and a bounded-length guard before the O(n\u00b2) base36 division; five reject KAT vectors pin the fail-closed boundary.
- **`ipns::record`** \u2014 protobuf-minimal V2 record: `signatureV2` over `\"ipns-signature:\" || data`, deprecated compat fields emitted, byte-stable unmarshal/marshal preserves every unknown field; five checks added to the frozen error surface.
- **`payload::pointer` / `payload::mailbox`** \u2014 symmetric-seal pointer payload bound by `pointer-payload` structured AAD, and HPKE mailbox with sender ECDSA identity sig inside the seal; both consume the structure-tag registry from #673 without redefining it.

<h3>Confidence Score: 4/5</h3>

Safe to merge. All three crypto paths (name codec, V2 record verify chain, pointer/mailbox seal-open) are correct and covered by KAT vectors. Two cosmetic inconsistencies exist but neither affects correctness or the security boundary.

The verify chain and seal/open paths are well-constructed and the KAT manifest self-verifies every vector before writing. Two minor inconsistencies were found: IpnsRecord::drop zeroizes f.raw but leaves the parallel FieldValue::Bytes allocation un-zeroized, and mailbox.rs maps a wrong-length senderSig to IdentitySignatureInvalid (Trust class) while pointer.rs maps the same structural condition to InvalidFieldLength (Malformed class). Neither affects the cryptographic guarantees or the gate's fail-closed behaviour on the happy path.

crates/core/src/ipns/record.rs (Drop zeroize completeness) and crates/core/src/payload/mailbox.rs (senderSig length classification vs pointer.rs).

